### Phase 4a.1 — Attach Evidence to Risk Assessments (IA only)

> **Still logged in as:** `auditor@fcc.go.tz` / `Pass@1234`
> *(SRS §1.8.1: "The system shall support attachment of evidence — policies, reports, data extracts — to support risk ratings")*
>
> **⚠️ Only the IA can upload or delete evidence. CIA can only view it.**
> **⚠️ Evidence cannot be added after an assessment is `approved` (terminal state).**

**Page:** `http://localhost:3001/service/grc/risk-assessments` → ⋮ → **View** on any assessment

In the detail dialog, scroll to the **Evidence Attachments** section at the bottom:

1. Click **Upload Evidence**
2. Select any supporting file (policy document, data extract, spreadsheet, etc.)
3. The file is uploaded to the **Document Records Service (DRS)** — GRC stores only the document UUID reference
4. The uploaded file appears in the list with filename, size, and date

**Suggested sample files to attach** (one per assessment):

| Assessment | Suggested Evidence File | Description |
|---|---|---|
| ICT Directorate | Any PDF or DOCX | e.g. "ICT Risk Register 2025.pdf" |
| Finance Unit | Any spreadsheet or PDF | e.g. "Finance Audit Findings Q2.xlsx" |
| Dar es Salaam Zone | Any document | e.g. "Zone Compliance Report.pdf" |
| Procurement Process | Any document | e.g. "PPA Compliance Checklist.docx" |

**What to verify:**
- File appears in the list immediately after upload ✅
- File size and upload date are shown ✅
- Trash icon is visible (IA can remove evidence before the assessment is approved) ✅
- After uploading, re-open the View dialog — file is still listed (persisted via DRS) ✅

> **Backend:** `POST /api/v1/grc/audit/risk-assessments/{id}/evidence/` (multipart/form-data)
> **Storage:** DRS tags the document as `document_type: audit_working_paper`, `classification: confidential`, retention 7 years

