## Phase 5 — Create Audit Plan (RBIAP)

> **Terminology used in this phase:**
> - **IA** = Internal Auditor = `auditor@fcc.go.tz` — *drafts* the plan
> - **CIA** = Chief Internal Auditor = `cia@fcc.go.tz` — *reviews and approves* the plan
>
> They are two different people. The IA creates and submits. The CIA reviews and pushes it through management, committee, and commission.

> **Who does what:**
> | Step | Who | Login |
> |---|---|---|
> | 1. Generate / Create draft plan | IA | `auditor@fcc.go.tz` |
> | 2. Edit draft — fill resource allocation, review priority areas | IA | `auditor@fcc.go.tz` |
> | 3. Submit for Approval ← **IA's role ends here** | IA | `auditor@fcc.go.tz` |
> | 4. WO Stage 1 — CIA Review | CIA | `cia@fcc.go.tz` |
> | 5. WO Stage 2 — Management Review | Management | `management@fcc.go.tz` |
> | 6. WO Stage 3 — Audit Committee Review | Audit Committee | `auditcommittee@fcc.go.tz` |
> | 7. WO Stage 4 — Commission Noting | Commission | `commission@fcc.go.tz` |
> | 8. Edit if Audit Committee returns for improvement | CIA | `cia@fcc.go.tz` |
>
> **Key rule:** While the plan is in `draft` status, the IA can edit it freely — this is when they fill resource allocation, review priority areas, etc. The moment the IA clicks **Submit for Approval**, the plan moves out of `draft` and the IA can no longer edit it. From that point, all actions belong to CIA, Management, Audit Committee, and Commission.
>
> **The IA does NOT appear in the 4-stage WO workflow (steps 4–7).** Per SRS Step 3, once the IA submits, the approval chain is entirely CIA → Management → Audit Committee → Commission.

---

### Button Visibility Rules (SRS-aligned)

| Button | IA (`auditor`) | CIA (`cia`) | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Generate from Risk Assessments** | ✅ visible | ❌ hidden | SRS Req 2: IA drafts the plan |
| **Create Audit Plan** (manual) | ✅ visible | ❌ hidden | SRS Req 2: IA drafts the plan |
| **Edit** button on list | ✅ draft plans only | ✅ any status | SRS Req 7: CIA improves after Audit Committee returns |
| **Delete** button on list | ✅ | ❌ hidden | IA owns drafting cycle |

---

### ⭐ Primary Path — Auto-Generate from Risk Assessments (SRS Req 40)

> **Login as:** `auditor@fcc.go.tz` / `Pass@1234`

> **SRS Requirement 40:** *"Automatically generate a prioritized, risk-based audit plan draft based on the assessment results."*

**Page:** Sidebar → **Audit Plans** → Click **"Generate from Risk Assessments"** button

**Pre-conditions (enforced by backend):**
- Audit Universe must be `approved` → error `UNIVERSE_NOT_APPROVED` if not
- No plan may already exist for the same universe + fiscal year → error `PLAN_EXISTS` if duplicate
- At least one approved risk assessment must exist for entities in the universe → error `NO_ASSESSMENTS` if none

> **⚠️ Only `approved` risk assessments feed into the plan.** Complete Phase 4c first (IA finalizes all 4 assessments to `approved`) so all 4 entities appear ranked in the generated plan.

**Steps:**
1. Navigate to GRC → **Audit Plans**
2. Click **Generate from Risk Assessments** — a dialog opens
3. Select:
   - **Fiscal Year:** `2025/2026`
   - **Audit Universe:** *(select the approved universe from Phase 2)*
4. Click **Generate** → page navigates to the new plan detail

**What the backend auto-populates (`POST /api/v1/grc/audit/plans/generate-draft/`):**
| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| `reference_number` | Auto-assigned as `RBIAP-{year_code}-001` |
| `title` | `Risk-Based Internal Audit Plan 2025/2026` |
| `plan_type` | `annual` |
| `status` | `draft` |
| `priority_areas` | All approved risk assessment entities sorted by `calculated_weighted_score` descending (highest risk first) — each entry includes rank, entity name, risk rating, and scores |
| `resource_allocation` | `{}` — intentionally empty; IA fills this before submitting |

**Expected:** Draft plan created. You land on the plan detail page.

---

