### Step 5b — Submit for Approval (IA)

> **Login as:** `auditor@fcc.go.tz` / `Pass@1234`
>
> **This is the last action the IA takes on this plan.** After clicking Submit, the IA cannot edit the plan anymore — the approval chain passes to CIA → Management → Audit Committee → Commission.

1. On the plan detail page → click **Submit for Approval**
   - GRC sets plan status → `management_review`
   - Work Orchestration starts its 4-stage workflow at the CIA Review stage

---

### Step 5c — 4-Stage Approval Workflow (CIA → Management → Committee → Commission)

> **The IA does not participate in this workflow.** Switch users as shown below.

| # | WO stage_key | Stage Name | Login As | Action Button |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `cia_review` | CIA Review | `cia@fcc.go.tz` | **Approve** / Return |
| 2 | `management_review` | Management Review | `management@fcc.go.tz` | **Adopt** / Request Changes |
| 3 | `committee_review` | Audit Committee Review | `auditcommittee@fcc.go.tz` | **Approve** / Request Improvement |
| 4 | `commission_noting` | Commission Noting | `commission@fcc.go.tz` (Rose Kimaro) | **Note** *(not "Approve")* |

After all 4 stages complete → GRC plan status → `approved`

> **If Audit Committee returns for improvement (SRS Step 8):** CIA logs in (`cia@fcc.go.tz`) → uses the **Edit** button (visible to CIA at any status) → makes improvements → Save → resubmit to committee.

> **Rejection path:** If rejected at any stage, GRC resets plan status to `draft` and clears `workflow_plan_id`. IA must resubmit from scratch.

