## Phase 7d — Engagement Notification (GAP 1 — SRS Req 10–14, 18)

> **Who does what:**
> | Step | Login As | Action |
> |---|---|---|
> | Create + Submit | `auditor@fcc.go.tz` | LA prepares EN → clicks **Submit for Approval** in EN dialog |
> | Approve | `cia@fcc.go.tz` | CIA opens the EN row → EN dialog shows **Approve** button → click it |
> | Transmit | `auditor@fcc.go.tz` | LA clicks **Transmit** in EN dialog (after EN is `approved`) |

**Page:** Sidebar → GRC → **Audit Engagements** → click your engagement row → **Engagement Detail page** → scroll to the **Engagement Notification** card → click **Add**

> **SRS §1.8.3 Steps 10–12:** After the audit program is approved, the Lead Auditor prepares the Engagement Notification (EN) — a formal notice to the auditable area. The CIA approves it (1-stage WO workflow) via the WO console, and the Lead Auditor then transmits it to the auditee.
> **Model:** `EngagementNotification` is OneToOneField per engagement — only one EN can exist per engagement. The **Add** button only appears when no EN exists yet; once created, click the EN row to view or manage it.
> **GAP 9 (FIXED):** After the EN reaches `approved` status, DRS stamps the document in-place with QR code + CIA signature. `document_id` is stored on the EN record and included in the API response. A **"Download Approved EN"** button appears in the EN detail dialog once the EN is `approved` or `transmitted`.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Engagement** (`audit_engagement_id`) | `ICT General Controls Audit 2025/2026` *(auto-populated from the engagement detail page)* |
| **Audit Period Start** (`audit_period_start`) | `2026-03-01` |
| **Audit Period End** (`audit_period_end`) | `2026-04-30` |
| **Notification Date** (`notification_date`) | *(leave blank — auto-set to today's date on Transmit — GAP E fixed)* |
| **Scope Summary** (`scope_summary`) | `ICT General Controls — access management, change management, backup and recovery, network security configuration.` |

**Expected result:** EN created with status `draft`. It appears in the **Engagement Notification** card on the Engagement Detail page.

### Status Workflow (1-stage WO workflow — CIA approval — SRS Steps 10–14):

> **Note:** The EN detail dialog (opened by clicking the EN row) contains all lifecycle action buttons:
> - **Edit** — visible in `draft` status (auditor only)
> - **Submit for Approval** — visible in `draft` status (auditor only); triggers the WO workflow
> - **Approve** — visible in `under_review` status (CIA only); directly advances the WO stage
> - **Transmit** — visible in `approved` status (auditor only); finalises the EN

1. Click the EN row → EN detail dialog opens → click **Submit for Approval**
   - Backend: `POST /engagement-notifications/{id}/submit/`
   - EN status immediately set to `under_review` by the service
   - Work Orchestration starts a **1-stage** CIA approval workflow
2. Log in as CIA (`cia@fcc.go.tz`) → open the engagement → click the EN row → click **Approve** in the detail dialog
   - Backend: `POST /engagement-notifications/{id}/workflow-action/` `{ action: 'approve' }`
   - WO workflow stage `cia_approval` is completed

| # | WO stage_key | Stage Name | Frontend Action |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `cia_approval` | CIA Approval | **Approve** button in EN dialog (CIA sees it when status is `under_review`) |

3. After WO final approval → Kafka event → GRC `notification.status = approved`
4. Click **Transmit** to formally send the EN to the auditee
   - Backend: `POST /engagement-notifications/{id}/transmit/`
   - Status updates to `transmitted`

**Full status progression:**

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `draft` | EN created, not yet submitted |
| `under_review` | Submitted — WO workflow running (CIA review) |
| `approved` | WO approved — ready to transmit |
| `transmitted` | Formally sent to auditee |

> **Return path:** If the CIA returns/rejects at the `cia_approval` stage → Kafka event → GRC resets `notification.status = draft`, clears `workflow_plan_id`. The **Submit for Approval** button reappears in the EN detail dialog.

### ✅ GAP 9 Stamp + Download Verification:
After status → `approved`:
1. Click the EN row in the **Engagement Notification** card → detail dialog opens
2. A **"Download Approved EN"** button is visible in the dialog (requires `document_id` to be set — it is set automatically on submit)
3. Click **Download Approved EN** → PDF downloads with CIA signature + QR code stamped
4. The same button remains visible after transmit (`transmitted` status)

> **How it works:** On Submit → GRC calls DRS to generate the EN PDF (`document_id` stored). On CIA Approval → Kafka consumer calls DRS stamp endpoint using service account auth → PDF is stamped in-place. `document_id` is included in the API response so the frontend can offer the download.

