## Phase 7e — Declaration of Independence (GAP 2 — SRS Req 16, 18, 38)

> **Login as:** `auditor@fcc.go.tz` / `Pass@1234` *(Internal Auditor / Lead Auditor — each team member creates and signs their own declaration)*
>
> *SRS §1.8.3: Each audit team member must sign a Declaration of Independence before participating in an engagement.*

**Page:** Sidebar → GRC → **Audit Engagements** → click your engagement → **Engagement Detail page** → scroll to the **Declarations** card → click **Add**

> **How the full flow works (all implemented):**
> 1. You create a declaration → backend immediately generates a PDF and uploads it to DRS → `document_id` is set automatically (you don't see this, it happens in the background)
> 2. You click **Sign** → `is_signed = true`, `status = signed`
> 3. When **all** declarations for the engagement are signed → backend calls DRS `generate-approved-stamp` → DRS overlays QR code (bottom-left) + CIA signature (bottom-right) on the last page of the PDF → `stamped_document_url` is set
>
> **All declarations must be `signed`** before the **Start Engagement Workflow** button will work. If any are still `pending`, the backend returns `DECLARATIONS_NOT_SIGNED` (400).

---

### Declaration — Create Your Declaration

> **⚠️ One declaration per user per engagement.** The backend enforces `unique_together = ['audit_engagement', 'declarant_user_id']`. If you try to create a second declaration as the same user for the same engagement, the API returns a 400 validation error. Create **one** declaration only.
>
> Since this test environment has only one internal auditor (Mary Simba — `auditor@fcc.go.tz`), only **one declaration** is needed and only one is possible. Do **Declaration A** (standard case — required for the flow). Use **Declaration B** as an alternative if you want to test the conflict field *instead*.

---

#### Declaration A — No Conflict *(Standard — use this one)*

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Engagement** | `ICT General Controls Audit 2025/2026` *(auto-populated from the engagement page)* |
| **I am independent** toggle | `ON` *(default — `has_conflict = false`)* |
| **Conflict Details** | *(leave empty)* |
| **Declaration Text** | *(pre-filled standard text — do not change)* |

**Expected result after saving:**
- Declaration row appears in the Declarations card with status `pending`
- `declarant_name` auto-filled from the logged-in user
- In the background: a PDF is generated and uploaded to DRS → `document_id` is now set on the record
- *(Verify via API if needed: `GET /api/v1/grc/declarations/?audit_engagement={id}` → `document_id` should not be null)*

---

#### Declaration B — With Conflict *(Alternative edge-case test — use INSTEAD of A, not in addition)*

> Skip this if you already created Declaration A. Creating both for the same user will fail with a 400 error.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Engagement** | `ICT General Controls Audit 2025/2026` |
| **I am independent** toggle | `OFF` → `conflict_details` field appears |
| **Conflict Details** | `I have a financial relationship with ICT Solutions Ltd, one of the vendors being reviewed in this engagement. I declare this conflict for CIA awareness and decision.` |

**Expected result after saving:**
- Declaration created with `has_conflict = true`, `conflict_details` populated, status `pending`
- PDF generated and uploaded to DRS in the background (same as Declaration A)

---

### Sign Your Declaration

1. In the **Declarations** card, click the declaration row → **Declaration detail dialog** opens
2. Click **Sign Declaration** inside the dialog
3. Status updates: `pending → signed`, `is_signed = true`, `signed_at` is set
4. The **Sign Declaration** button disappears — replaced by a **Signed** badge

> **⚠️ The Sign button is inside the detail dialog** — click the declaration row first to open the dialog, then click Sign.

**After signing (since only one declarant → all declarations are signed immediately):**
- Backend detects all declarations signed → calls DRS `generate-approved-stamp` on each declaration that has `document_id` set
- DRS overlays QR code (bottom-left) + CIA signature (bottom-right) on the PDF → `stamped_document_url` is saved back to the declaration
- The detail dialog stays open and shows the **"View stamped declaration ↗"** link — no page reload needed

