## Phase 14 — Create Audit Meetings

> **Login as:** `auditor@fcc.go.tz` / `Pass@1234` for all meeting steps *(Lead Auditor — SRS §1.8.3 Steps 14, 17, 20, 24)*

---

### How Meetings Connect to Engagements

Meetings are always **linked to an Audit Engagement**. There are two ways to access them:

| Method | Path | When to use |
|--------|------|-------------|
| **Via Engagement Detail page** | Sidebar → **Audit Engagements** → find your engagement → click **View** (eye icon) → go to the **Meetings** tab | Recommended — you stay in context of the engagement |
| **Via the Meetings sidebar entry** | Sidebar → GRC → **Meetings** → Click **Create** | Also works — you must select the engagement from the dropdown |

> **✅ The Engagement Detail page has a Meetings tab (GAP-3).** All meetings for the engagement are visible there with their status, type, and date. You can create new meetings directly from this tab — you do not need to go to the separate Meetings page.

**Engagement phase gates — when each meeting type is allowed:**

| Meeting Type | UI Label | SRS Step | Engagement must be in phase |
|---|---|---|---|
| `entry` | Entry Conference | Step 14 | `fieldwork` **only** |
| `pre_exit` | Pre-Exit Conference | Step 17 | `fieldwork` or `reporting` |
| `team` | Audit Team Meeting | Step 20 | `fieldwork` or `reporting` |
| `exit` | Exit Conference | Step 24 | `reporting` or `completed` |

> **⚠️ Entry meeting requires `fieldwork` phase only** — not `planning`. The Engagement Notification must have been transmitted (which advances the engagement to `fieldwork`) before an entry meeting can be created. Creating one while the engagement is still `planning` returns `INVALID_ENGAGEMENT_PHASE`.

> **⚠️ Pre-exit meeting requires at least one approved Working Paper (GAP-8).** If no WP has `review_status = 'approved'`, you get `PRE_EXIT_REQUIRES_APPROVED_WPS`. Complete Phase 8 Steps A–D (WPs approved) before creating the pre-exit meeting.

> **⚠️ Duplicate prevention (GAP-4).** Only one active (non-cancelled) meeting per type per engagement is allowed. A second `entry` meeting returns `DUPLICATE_MEETING_TYPE`.

> **⚠️ API note:** `meeting_type` short values: `entry`, `pre_exit`, `team`, `exit`. The UI shows full display labels.

> **⚠️ `scheduled_date`** — The UI shows two separate **Date** and **Time** fields. They combine into ISO DateTime on submit (e.g. `2026-03-01T09:00:00`).

---

### Meeting 1: Entry Conference (`entry` type)

**Pre-condition:** Engagement must be in `fieldwork` phase. Step 15 in the Execution Order (Start Engagement Workflow → WO Stage 1 → **Start Fieldwork**) must be completed first.

#### Step A — Create (Scheduled)

**Navigate to:** Sidebar → **Audit Engagements** → find `ICT General Controls Audit 2025/2026` → click **View** → go to **Meetings** tab → click **Create Meeting**

*(Or: Sidebar → **Meetings** → **Create** → select engagement from the dropdown)*

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Engagement** | `ICT General Controls Audit 2025/2026` *(auto-filled if creating from the Engagement Detail page)* |
| **Meeting Type** | `entry` *(UI shows "Entry Conference")* |
| **Meeting Title** | `ICT Audit Entry Conference — March 2026` |
| **Scheduled Date** | `2026-03-01` |
| **Scheduled Time** | `09:00` *(UI combines → `2026-03-01T09:00:00`)* |
| **Location** | `ICT Directorate Board Room, HQ Building, 3rd Floor` |
| **Agenda** | `1. Introduction of audit team members and scope of the engagement\n2. Presentation of audit objectives and methodology\n3. Overview of key risk areas identified during planning\n4. Discussion of audit timeline and key milestones\n5. Logistics: document requests, staff availability, access requirements\n6. Questions from ICT Directorate management` |

**Expected result:** Meeting created with status `scheduled`. Reference number auto-generated: `MTG-ENG-2025-001-ENTRY-001`.

> **✅ GAP-6 auto-sync:** After creation, open the Engagement Detail — `entry_meeting_date` on the engagement record is automatically updated to `2026-03-01T09:00:00`.

#### Step B — Progress to In Progress

Click **Progress Update** (or ⋮ → **Progress Update**) → select `in_progress`.

> **⚠️ Once `in_progress`, structural fields are LOCKED** (Engagement, Type, Title, Date, Location, Agenda). Only post-meeting fields remain editable: Minutes, Key Discussions, Clarifications, Agreed Observations, Attendees, and document uploads.

#### Step C — Record Post-Meeting Data

Click **⋮ menu → Edit** while meeting is `in_progress`:

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Minutes** | `The entry conference was held on 1 March 2026 at 09:00hrs. The Lead Auditor introduced the audit team and presented the audit scope, objectives and methodology. ICT Directorate management acknowledged the audit timeline and committed to providing requested documents within 5 working days. Key logistics were agreed including room allocation and staff availability schedule.` |
| **Key Discussions** | `1. Audit scope confirmed — access controls, change management, backup and recovery in scope.\n2. ICT Director committed to designating a liaison officer by 3 March 2026.\n3. Document request list to be submitted by audit team within 2 working days.\n4. Audit timeline: fieldwork 1–28 March, preliminary findings 5 April.` |
| **Clarifications** | *(leave blank — only used for Pre-Exit meetings)* |
| **Agreed Observations** | *(leave blank — only used for Pre-Exit meetings)* |

**Attendees** — click **Add Attendee** for each row:

| Name | Title/Position | Role | Present |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Mary Simba` | `Lead Auditor` | `auditor` | ✅ Yes |
| `David Omondi` | `Audit Team Member` | `auditor` | ✅ Yes |
| `ICT Director` | `Director of ICT` | `auditee` | ✅ Yes |
| `ICT Systems Manager` | `Systems Manager` | `auditee` | ✅ Yes |

Click **Update Meeting** → saved.

#### Step D — Complete the Meeting

Click **Progress Update** → select `completed`.

> **⚠️ Minutes text must be non-empty** before `completed` is allowed — backend returns `MINUTES_REQUIRED` otherwise.

**Expected result:** Status → `completed`.

> **✅ GAP-9 auto-PDF on completion:** The backend automatically generates two PDFs and uploads them to DRS:
> 1. **Meeting Minutes PDF** (`minutes_document_id` set on the meeting)
> 2. **Attendance Register PDF** (`attendance_document_id` set on the meeting)
>
> Verify: `docker logs fims-grc-service 2>&1 | grep "GAP-9"`
> Expected log lines:
> - `GAP-9: Minutes PDF for meeting … uploaded to DRS as document …`
> - `GAP-9: Attendance PDF for meeting … uploaded to DRS as document …`
>
> The API response data will contain non-null `minutes_document_id` and `attendance_document_id`.

